              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "In the **2025\u201326 NBA season (2026 playoffs)**, the Indiana Pacers **did not qualify** for the postseason. After reaching the NBA Finals the previous year, the Pacers suffered a difficult, injury-plagued season (finishing 14th in the East with a 19\u201363 record), largely due to star guard Tyrese Haliburton missing the entire year after tearing his Achilles tendon in Game 7 of the 2025 NBA Finals.\n\nHowever, the Pacers had deep playoff runs in both **2025** and **2024**. Their playoff opponents and series results for those years are detailed below:\n\n### **2025 NBA Playoffs (Reached the NBA Finals)**\n* **First Round:** Defeated the **Milwaukee Bucks** (4\u20131)\n* **Eastern Conference Semifinals:** Defeated the **Cleveland Cavaliers** (4\u20131)\n* **Eastern Conference Finals:** Defeated the **New York Knicks** (4\u20132)\n* **NBA Finals:** Lost to the **Oklahoma City Thunder** (3\u20134)\n\n---\n\n### **2024 NBA Playoffs (Reached the Eastern Conference Finals)**\n* **First Round:** Defeated the **Milwaukee Bucks** (4\u20132)\n* **Eastern Conference Semifinals:** Defeated the **New York Knicks** (4\u20133)\n* **Eastern Conference Finals:** Lost to the **Boston Celtics** (0\u20134)",
